/T (i. Implementing oil pollution, liability and compensation measures in West Africa)
/E (i. Implementing oil pollution, liability and compensation measures in West Africa)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/ActualText (Those responsible for implementing IMO conventions on pollution preparedness and response, and for transposing them into domestic legislation attended a subregional workshop aimed at sharing best practices relating to the instruments' application in West Africa.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/ActualText <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/ActualText (The meeting was delivered via IMO's Integrated Technical Coo-peration Programme \(ITCP\) under the framework of the Global Initiative for West, Central and Southern Africa \(GI WACAF\). It forms part of the Organization's commitment to supporting African Small Island Developing States \(SIDs\) and Least Deve-loped Countries \(LDCs\). Similar workshops were held remotely in 2021 for the benefit of Gambia, Liberia, Namibia and Nigeria - and in 2022, under the GI SEA Project, for Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, Indonesia, the Lao People's Democratic Republic, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Viet Nam.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
